 in Caldria. It now plans to cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. The plan is being cut because equity funding wasn't available (`pellham-offering`).\n- **Equity demand is weak across the sector.** Two other utility share offerings were cut back in size (`utility-credit`, Q3 2026).\n- **The funding need is large.** Pellham plans 2027 capex up 18% and Norvane up 12%, mostly on substations and transformers (`utility-capex-2027`). Equity can't cover that at current demand.\n- **Debt is the better route.** Bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, but Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (`utility-credit`). Debt is costlier but still open.\n\nI only found these three documents, so I have no numbers on equity valuations or on each utility's balance-sheet headroom. The conclusion rests on one failed deal, two downsized deals and one successful bond. Norvane's equity access hasn't been tested directly.\n\nThe practical effect is that capex plans funded by equity are likely to be trimmed or deferred, as Pellham's already have been. The related debt-market question is with n3 and n5.","ttft_ms":2175,"type":"result","duration_ms":19987,"uuid":"4656ddbe-569d-4274-89eb-f929782b784c","ttft_stream_ms":1727,"time_to_request_ms":60,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":13,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":4,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":2,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":9,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":62,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":182,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":108,"pro